      "conversation_id": "ai-conv-1",
      "role": "user",
      "content": "What are the key performance patterns for caching and streaming in Next.js 15?",
      "created_at": "2026-10-29T08:22:48.506Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "ai-msg-2",
      "conversation_id": "ai-conv-1",
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In Next.js 15, key architectural considerations include:\n\n1. **Uncached by Default**: `fetch` requests and route handlers are now uncached by default. Opt in explicitly with `cache: 'force-cache'`.\n2. **React 19 Actions**: Form submissions and mutations can use `useActionState` and Server Actions directly.\n3. **Suspense Boundaries**: Wrap async Server Components with fine-grained `<Suspense fallback={<Skeleton />}>` to unlock progressive HTML streaming.",
      "created_at": "2026-10-29T08:22:48.506Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "5fd6f125-ab83-4942-801b-b83a18368267",
